<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RM_GreySeaShoreScatter_Register.xml  TerminalBiomes · authored 2026-09-26
  ============================================================================
  GREYSEA_SHORE_MUTATOR_SPECIFICS_1 — the registration half.
  RM_GreySeaShoreScatter.xml declares RM_GreySeaScatterShoreDomes; a
  GenStepDef on its own runs on NO map. This file lists it.

  Same three-file shape and the same target as this mod's
  RUT_ScaldWreckScatter_Register.xml — read that header for the Core
  citation (Core/Defs/MapGeneration/BasePlayerMapGenerator.xml,
  MapGeneratorDef Name="Base_Player", <genSteps> a plain <li> list).

  SCOPE is safe to be global because the step's OWN terrain validator
  confines it: terrainValidationAllowed names RM_GreySaltCrust, a tag
  carried by exactly one terrain in the load order (RM_SaltCrustShore,
  RM_GreySeaTerrains.xml), which only the Grey Sea's shore ever lays. On
  every other map the step finds no valid cell and does nothing.

  ⛔ Do NOT also add this to the sea-dive generators. These are the domes
  ABOVE the waterline; the floor's own domes are RM_SaltDome, placed by
  RM_GreySeaScatterDomes, and the two are different defs on purpose (the
  shore one yields nothing — RULED, no harvestable shore salt).

  Conditional test xpath is IDENTICAL to the inner Add's xpath, this mod's
  own discipline: if Core ever renames Base_Player or restructures the node
  this becomes a silent no-op rather than a red error.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>RM_GreySeaScatterShoreDomes</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
